course: dictionary
lesson: 178
title: Ahead: in front, later, or winning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Ahead» is a small word with three main jobs. It can mean in front, still to come, or winning.
explain: «The Rat walks ahead, his shoulders humped, his eyes fixed on the straight grey road.» The Rat is in front, further along the road. When you read «ahead», ask: in front of what?
explain: «Ahead» can also mean the future. In «plan ahead» or «look ahead», you think about what is still to come. In a game, if you have more points, you are ahead.
fact: Ahead is an adverb, so it tells you where, when or how something happens.
fact: «Ahead» means in front, or further on.
fact: «Ahead» can mean in the future, still to come.
fact: «Ahead of» means in front of: you can be ahead of the others in a race.
fact: «Go ahead» means you may start or do it.
exercise: «The Rat walks ahead, his eyes fixed on the straight grey road.» What does ahead mean here? | *In front | Lost on the road | Far away from home | Finished with the walk
exercise: In a game, Sam has 20 points and Jo has 15. What does «Sam is ahead» mean? | *Sam is winning, with more points | Sam is asleep | Sam has lost his shoes | Sam is running backwards
exercise: The teacher says, «Go ahead.» What does she mean? | Go to bed early | *You may start or do it | Go home now | Stop at once
test: Mia wants to finish her homework early, so she will plan ahead. What does plan ahead mean? | Forget about it until the last minute | *Think about and prepare for what is still to come | Do it backwards | Sleep all day
test: When you stream a film, a little is stored «ahead». What does ahead mean here? | Stored upside down | *Stored in advance, further on than the part you are watching | Stored at the very end of the film | Stored in the bin
exam: Which meaning fits «Europe pulled ahead in the 1800s»? | Europe fell behind and went to sleep | *Europe got in front of other places and moved further along | Europe stopped trading altogether | Europe was lost on a long road
